    read:`<div class="exam-panel" style="--c:167,139,250;"><header class="ep-h"><span class="ep-tag">lectura · Social Media: Friend or Foe?</span><span class="ep-count">4 preguntas</span></header><div class="reading-text" style="font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink-2);margin-bottom:12px;max-height:160px;overflow-y:auto;"><b>Social Media: Friend or Foe?</b><br>Social media platforms have become integral to modern life, connecting billions of people across the globe. Proponents argue that these platforms foster community, enable rapid information sharing, and provide economic opportunities for content creators. Critics, however, point to rising rates of anxiety and depression among heavy users, particularly adolescents who are still developing their identity and self-esteem. Research from Harvard Medical School suggests that passive consumption — scrolling without interacting — is significantly more harmful than active engagement. The debate continues, with governments worldwide considering regulatory frameworks.</div><div class="tf-q"><p style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">Social media connects billions of people globally.</p><div class="tf-btns"><button class="tf-btn" data-val="T">TRUE</button><button class="tf-btn" data-val="F">FALSE</button></div></div><div class="tf-q"><p style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">All research shows social media only harms young people.</p><div class="tf-btns"><button class="tf-btn" data-val="T">TRUE</button><button class="tf-btn" data-val="F">FALSE</button></div></div><div class="tf-q"><p style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">Passive scrolling is more harmful than active engagement.</p><div class="tf-btns"><button class="tf-btn" data-val="T">TRUE</button><button class="tf-btn" data-val="F">FALSE</button></div></div><div class="tf-q"><p style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">Governments are ignoring social media regulation.</p><div class="tf-btns"><button class="tf-btn" data-val="T">TRUE</button><button class="tf-btn" data-val="F">FALSE</button></div></div></div>`,
